# The paths a pull request needs the maintainer's label read-by-maintainer to change (#271): the
# required status maintainer-read is red on a pull request that changes one of them until the
# maintainer has set the label himself, and every new push removes it. scripts/maintainer-read.py
# reads this file from the base branch, and only the forms it documents. The workflow and the script
# are the same files as in astrapi69/mystic-crypt-ui, whose MaintainerReadCheckTest covers them.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately not enabled: every pull request comes from the
# account astrapi69, which is the owner named here, and GitHub does not let an author approve his
# own pull request. This file is the marking and the single list of the paths, nothing more.

# the consensus and signature rules: what a valid block and transaction are, and how they are signed
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/ConsensusRules.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/Genesis.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/GenesisAnchor.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/SignatureSuite.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/SigningPayload.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/TransactionSigner.java @astrapi69
/src/main/java/io/github/astrapi69/lethenon/DeterministicKeys.java @astrapi69

# the check itself, so that a pull request cannot loosen it without the label
/.github/CODEOWNERS @astrapi69
/.github/workflows/maintainer-read.yml @astrapi69
/scripts/maintainer-read.py @astrapi69
